    {'para': '**185. Feminine Substantives in ⟨i⟩ and ⟨u⟩** are declined as in the paradigms on the next page. The two series of forms exhibit complete parallelism: where the one shows ⟨i⟩, ⟨y⟩, ⟨e⟩, or ⟨ay⟩, the other shows respectively ⟨u⟩, ⟨v⟩, ⟨o⟩, or ⟨av⟩; cf. §§ 50, 51. In the D., Ab.-G., and L. sing., these stems sometimes follow ⟨nadī⟩; thus ⟨matyai⟩, ⟨-yās⟩, ⟨-yām⟩; ⟨dhenvai⟩, ⟨-vās⟩, ⟨-vām⟩.'},
