    {'para': '**187.** Adjectives in ⟨i⟩ and ⟨u⟩ are often inflected in the feminine like ⟨mati⟩ and ⟨dhenu⟩. But adjectives in ⟨u⟩ preceded by one consonant often form a derivative feminine stem by adding ⟨ī⟩. Thus, ⟨bahu⟩ ‘much’, N. masc. ⟨bahus⟩, f. ⟨bahvī⟩, n. ⟨bahu⟩; ⟨guru⟩ ‘heavy’, m. ⟨gurus⟩, f. ⟨gurvī⟩, n. ⟨guru⟩. This fem. is then declined like ⟨nadī⟩.'},
